{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5waShdgYdRVzeu9gHv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rewrote `metrics/counter.py` so increments are no longer lost and `snapshot()` is consistent. `tests/test_metrics.py` passed on all 5 runs, but that's the only test, and it covers increments from threads, not `snapshot()`.\n\nThe cause was `incr` reading the value, yielding, then writing it back with no lock, so concurrent increments overwrote each other. `snapshot()` copied the dict while other threads could still be inserting keys.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **Per-counter locks:** each name now has its own small cell with its own lock. `incr` does its read-modify-write under that lock, so different counters never block each other.\n- **Registry lock:** a separate lock guards only the name-to-cell mapping, and `incr` holds it just long enough to look up or create a cell.\n- **`snapshot()`:** it builds a plain dict while holding the registry lock, so the dict can't change size during the copy. Each value is read whole, but the copy isn't one atomic view across all counters.\n- **`reset()`:** it drops cells instead of zeroing them, so `snapshot()` still omits reset names as before. An `incr` that already holds a dropped cell counts as having happened before the reset.\n\nThe public API (`incr`, `get`, `snapshot`, `reset`) is unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2474,"cache_read_input_tokens":34559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2474},"output_tokens":428,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23cfbe06-db22-4022-b6fb-e12e451b257d","uuid":"f9c3decf-de12-4070-b90e-9ce0ee0c679e","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:49:59.222Z","request_id":"req_011C